            <ArticleTitle>[Myocardial bridging--symptoms of coronary disease that sometimes is not].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1923-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Presumed innocent: typical chest pain and a positive stress test, but normal coronary arteries at first sight; this is the typical pattern of myocardial bridging. We present a interesting case report and details about diagnosis and therapy that nowadays should be offered to such patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
